# Build context for the DASHBOARD image only.
#
# BuildKit gives a Dockerfile its own ignore file when one is named after it,
# which is what lets the production `.dockerignore` stay exactly as strict as it
# is. That file is written for the API image and it excludes three things this
# build cannot do without: `dashboard/`, `requirements-dashboard.txt`, and
# `.streamlit/` -- the last one named explicitly, because the API has no pages
# to render and no reason to carry a Streamlit config.
#
# Without this file every one of those COPY instructions would find nothing and
# the build would fail. Same deny-by-default posture, same credential
# exclusions; only the allow-list differs, and it differs because the two images
# ship different products.

*

# --- what the dashboard image actually needs --------------------------------
# The package, which the app puts on sys.path itself rather than installing.
!src/

# The pages.
!dashboard/

# The hardening configuration. `showErrorDetails`, `toolbarMode` and
# `gatherUsageStats` are security settings: an image built without this file
# renders tracebacks, and their absolute paths, into a visitor's browser.
!.streamlit/

# The dependency manifests. Both, because the first includes the second.
!requirements-dashboard.txt
!requirements-api.txt

# The persisted vector index. Demo traffic never opens it -- stub mode is BM25
# over FTS5 -- but hybrid retrieval needs it once a provider is configured.
!data/kb_vectors.db

# --- re-excluded, even under the paths added back above ---------------------
# `*` does not reach inside an un-ignored directory, so these need their own
# exclusions.
src/**/__pycache__/
src/**/*.pyc
src/**/*.pyo
dashboard/**/__pycache__/
dashboard/**/*.pyc
dashboard/**/*.pyo

# --- never, under any circumstance ------------------------------------------
# Already covered by `*`. Named anyway, because this file is read by people
# deciding whether a secret can reach the daemon, and "it is implied by a
# wildcard three screens up" is not the answer that question deserves.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
.git/
.gitignore
secrets/
**/secrets/
